# Release Notes Generation Rule
When asked to generate release notes:
1. Always inspect the current git diff against HEAD (`git diff HEAD`).
2. Group changes into:
   - **Features** (user-facing additions)
   - **Bug Fixes** (resolved issues)
   - **Performance & Refactoring** (internal improvements)
   - **Config / Dependencies** (dependency bumps, environment tweaks)
3. Reference specific filenames and key functions modified.
4. Keep entries concise, high-signal, and devoid of vague fluff.